Expected elements: present

Every must-show item renders and no must-not-show item appears: full hash, `Succeeded`, the neutral `Not observable` chip with the published reason, exactly one provenance marker (the `Data` row badge `Real Aztec mainnet data` at the top of the Overview grid — no band, no chip), permanence stated verbatim, internal calls and state changes both "permanently, not yet", the footer closing the page with all three drawn marks. No retry, spinner, disabled control, trace reference or error colour anywhere. It reads as correct, not broken.

All five changes landed. Cost is base ten; the decoded-input note now uses the third state honestly; `Age`/`Type` rows are labelled; the note spans the grid flush-left and that reads deliberate; the chain is `/aztec`. Read beside `tx-detail--absent`, the two reasons stay distinct — pruning versus private kernel — so the pages do not collapse.

What fails is tone, and it fails by leaking machine tokens into prose. The label `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` (y1245) is a camelCase key uppercased; the value is 19 undelimited digits plus `FeeJuice`; `TYPE` prints the bare enum `public` (y1102) beside sentence-case chips; the breadcrumb calls the chain `aztec` (y166) while the badge 640px below calls it Aztec mainnet. The Data row then shouts `NO TRANSACTION INSIDE IT WAS REPLAYABLE` (y860) and prints `transaction(s)`/`block(s)`.

Fix first: humanise the cost label/value and the breadcrumb chain name; drop the all-caps clause and the template plurals.

Rating: 6/10

